00:04:47.010 --> 00:04:48.750
So wait, you're originally
from Benin, right?

00:04:48.750 --> 00:04:49.583
West Africa?

00:04:49.583 --> 00:04:52.020
- Benin Republic, West Africa.

00:04:52.020 --> 00:04:53.460
I had a-

00:04:53.460 --> 00:04:55.110
- [Kelly] Was it hard to adjust?

00:04:55.110 --> 00:04:55.943
- You kidding me?

00:04:55.943 --> 00:04:58.470
- Yeah, I'm from Texas
and it was hard for me

00:04:58.470 --> 00:04:59.433
to adjust here.

00:05:00.420 --> 00:05:04.860
- Benin Republic so I was
sent to Europe, to France

00:05:04.860 --> 00:05:07.050
to better my education, and it's there

00:05:07.050 --> 00:05:10.856
that I come to learn about movies.

00:05:10.856 --> 00:05:13.800
You know, more about movies in general,

00:05:13.800 --> 00:05:16.610
but really about superhero
movies, and so on and so forth.

00:05:16.610 --> 00:05:20.310
So I mean, my early days
of interaction with films

00:05:20.310 --> 00:05:25.310
came from a very young
age where every Wednesday

00:05:25.740 --> 00:05:28.200
we had off from school.

00:05:28.200 --> 00:05:32.370
So every Wednesday, all children
and all kids from school,

00:05:32.370 --> 00:05:34.800
I mean, would be off from
school and everybody,

00:05:34.800 --> 00:05:36.780
there's only one theater in that city.

00:05:36.780 --> 00:05:37.770
- [Kelly] Oh, so you'd all get together.

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:40.680
- And so we all get together
and go to the movie theater,

00:05:40.680 --> 00:05:45.367
and so you have the whole week
to collect detergent packages

00:05:45.367 --> 00:05:49.080
that you would recycle, and
that would give you a ticket to-

00:05:49.080 --> 00:05:50.097
- Oh, that's incredible.

00:05:50.097 --> 00:05:52.320
- And so it was incredible,

00:05:52.320 --> 00:05:54.660
and so but the theater will be so filled

00:05:54.660 --> 00:05:57.720
because imagine we're
talking about the capital.

00:05:57.720 --> 00:06:00.090
There's only one movie theater there,

00:06:00.090 --> 00:06:02.760
which was called Vogue at the time.

00:06:02.760 --> 00:06:03.960
- Who has the responsibility

00:06:03.960 --> 00:06:06.180
of picking that movie for everyone?

00:06:06.180 --> 00:06:07.620
- Well, you know, but it was interesting

00:06:07.620 --> 00:06:12.000
because the theater would be so filled

00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:13.080
all the way to the bathroom,

00:06:13.080 --> 00:06:16.050
all the way to the outside, to the walls,

00:06:16.050 --> 00:06:18.600
people, kids will be climbing walls

00:06:18.600 --> 00:06:22.830
to just hear the sound
of the film playing.

00:06:22.830 --> 00:06:24.780
And generally those film playing were-

00:06:24.780 --> 00:06:26.299
- It's magical.

00:06:26.299 --> 00:06:27.960
- It was magical for us.

00:06:27.960 --> 00:06:32.960
Those films were like Gary
Cooper, you know, cowboy.

00:06:33.030 --> 00:06:38.030
And all we could hear the
sound of the gun going off and-

00:06:39.330 --> 00:06:40.690
- Horses, all the stuff.

00:06:40.690 --> 00:06:42.453
- Shoes with the spurs, you know?

00:06:44.130 --> 00:06:45.933
- You're like, Americans are crazy.

00:06:47.190 --> 00:06:50.310
- But it was uplifting for us,

00:06:50.310 --> 00:06:52.950
and it was really a
different world, you know?

00:06:52.950 --> 00:06:53.913
- That's super magical.

00:06:53.913 --> 00:06:56.010
- That was absolutely magical for us.

00:06:56.010 --> 00:07:00.546
So that was my awakening to-

00:07:00.546 --> 00:07:01.504
- I love that.

00:07:01.504 --> 00:07:02.337
- To movies.

00:07:02.337 --> 00:07:03.660
And so when I got to Europe

00:07:03.660 --> 00:07:07.190
and understood more about television,

00:07:09.960 --> 00:07:11.760
seeing television, and seeing documentary

00:07:11.760 --> 00:07:12.810
and so on and so forth,

00:07:12.810 --> 00:07:15.720
so that's how I became more in love

00:07:15.720 --> 00:07:19.050
with the idea of being part of, you know,

00:07:19.050 --> 00:07:20.550
trying to do this as a career.

00:07:20.550 --> 00:07:21.750
- Yeah, 'cause it seems so magical.

00:07:21.750 --> 00:07:23.040
That's why I wanted to be a part of it.

00:07:23.040 --> 00:07:25.230
His new movie is "Shazam:
Fury of the Gods."

00:07:25.230 --> 00:07:26.063
So I love the movie.

00:07:26.063 --> 00:07:27.630
Could you explain your character

00:07:27.630 --> 00:07:29.760
and kind of what drew you to the role?

00:07:29.760 --> 00:07:33.330
- This idea of dealing with magic,

00:07:33.330 --> 00:07:35.910
and playing an ancient wizard,

00:07:35.910 --> 00:07:40.260
and the country I come
from, Benin Republic,

00:07:40.260 --> 00:07:44.763
is a place where magic and this idea

00:07:46.950 --> 00:07:51.100
of the forces of nature, we're very much

00:07:52.290 --> 00:07:53.880
very connected to that.

00:07:53.880 --> 00:07:55.490
- Which is real. Yeah.

00:07:55.490 --> 00:07:59.160
- And through this idea
of this way of life

00:07:59.160 --> 00:08:01.064
that's called voodoo.

00:08:01.064 --> 00:08:06.064
And voodoo over time had
suffered tremendous defamation.

00:08:08.640 --> 00:08:12.300
The notion is that this is a evil doing,

00:08:12.300 --> 00:08:16.470
evil way of practicing some
sort of like religious.

00:08:16.470 --> 00:08:18.210
- Well, that's a big bummer.

00:08:18.210 --> 00:08:22.740
- It sure is a big bummer,
but it was due to slavery.

00:08:22.740 --> 00:08:26.010
I've come to find out
when I finally decided

00:08:26.010 --> 00:08:29.040
because I wanted to understand

00:08:29.040 --> 00:08:32.340
why there was such a bad name.

00:08:32.340 --> 00:08:33.660
- Like negative connotation.

00:08:33.660 --> 00:08:36.090
- Negative connotation about voodoo,

00:08:36.090 --> 00:08:38.340
and so I wanted to do
a documentary about it

00:08:38.340 --> 00:08:40.230
because again, I come from a country

00:08:40.230 --> 00:08:42.550
in which, you know, now

00:08:44.670 --> 00:08:49.470
every January 10th, it's
a national celebration

00:08:49.470 --> 00:08:50.430
throughout the country.

00:08:50.430 --> 00:08:54.750
And even people from various
places in the diaspora

00:08:54.750 --> 00:08:57.870
meaning Cuba, Dominican Republic, Brazil,

00:08:57.870 --> 00:09:00.810
they travel all the way
to Benin to celebrate.

00:09:00.810 --> 00:09:04.039
- Wow, so the documentary
will kind of explain

00:09:04.039 --> 00:09:06.120
what it really is, right?

00:09:06.120 --> 00:09:09.300
- I tried, and I think this is one of

00:09:09.300 --> 00:09:10.530
the most challenging things

00:09:10.530 --> 00:09:14.490
I ever came trying to realize,

00:09:14.490 --> 00:09:18.600
and they don't really
like to talk about it.

00:09:18.600 --> 00:09:20.070
- God, I can't wait to
see this documentary.

00:09:20.070 --> 00:09:21.420
What's it called again?

00:09:21.420 --> 00:09:23.580
- "In Search of Spirit,
In Search of Voodoo."

00:09:23.580 --> 00:09:25.590
- In Search of Spirit,
In Search of Voodoo."

00:09:25.590 --> 00:09:26.733
Okay. Awesome.

